mechanism:
Inspect the current unfinished schedule, scene tree, navigation geometry, and live exclusion disc to identify the two required goals whose navigating access is broken. Change scene-tree transforms—of the affected destination geometry, a suitable enclosing sub-assembly, or the whole build as necessary—so that:

1. both required goals are outside the live exclusion disc and reachable by RVO-driven navigating agents;
2. their required transport, deposit, and lift sequence can close;
3. scene-tree nesting and required relative assembly geometry remain valid; and
4. no other still-required goal is made unreachable.

The exclusion disc is not edited, relaxed, moved, or deleted. The method of selecting feasible replacement poses is open; the required effect is restored navigating access while the restriction persists. The tool does not assign robots, formulate constraints, or invoke the MILP re-solve. It consumes intervention time and energy but no body spare. Preconditions are that the blocked goals and movable scene-tree transforms remain observable. The transform edit can be reversed before dependent physical work occurs; after cargo has been deposited or installed at the relocated geometry, reversal is not generally safe without an additional physical relocation.
